course: dictionary
lesson: 11032
title: Weak: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around «weak» to find the clue. «After the flu, Sam felt weak and could barely lift his bag» means weak has no energy in the body.
explain: «The Coriolis effect is too weak to decide which way water drains from a bath.» Here weak does not mean tired or easy to break. It means so small that it has no real effect.
explain: «Some reasons are weak, like "everyone does it".» Weak here means not good enough to convince people. The reason is poor, even though it sounds like a reason.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «feeling not good enough to convince» fits better than «feeling not strong», you have found the right meaning. Ask: what is the sentence really about, the body, the object, or the idea?
fact: Weak means not strong, with little power or energy in your body.
fact: Weak can mean easy to break, like a weak rope, or a drink with a lot of water and not much taste, like weak tea.
fact: A weak signal, light or sound is faint, so it is hard to see or hear.
fact: Weak can also mean not good at something, like a weak point in an argument.
fact: Useful phrases: «weak spot», «weak point», «grow weak». In science, a weak magnet attracts only from close by.
exercise: «After the illness, she still felt weak.» What does weak mean here? | Easy to break | Full of water | Faint and quiet | *Not having much energy
exercise: «The Coriolis effect is too weak to decide which way water drains from a bath.» What does weak mean here? | Full of water | Easy to break | *Too small to have a real effect | Not good at something
exercise: «Some reasons are weak, like "everyone does it".» What does weak suggest? | Full of water | Easy to break | *Not good enough to convince people | Strong and loud
test: «The old rope was weak, and it snapped under the load.» What does weak mean? | Full of flavour | Bright and shiny | Very strong | *Easy to break
test: «The tea was weak, with lots of water and hardly any taste.» What does weak mean? | *Has a lot of water and not much taste | Cold and sweet | Hot and bitter | Very strong
exam: Ella says, «The radio signal was weak, so the music was hard to hear.» What does weak mean here? | Easy to break | *Faint and quiet | Full of water | Very strong and clear
